<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hands-for-beast-mastery-hunter-dps">Hands for Beast Mastery Hunter DPS</h4>For the gloves it is the exact same situation as the shoulders and you will want to aim for <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=60307/lightning-charged-gloves">
<img alt="Lightning-Charged Gloves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_mail_raidhunter_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightning-Charged Gloves</span></a>. Getting T11 set bonuses is important for early dps. There's a very solid choice in <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=69939/dragonfire-gloves">
<img alt="Dragonfire Gloves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_mail_raidhunter_j_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dragonfire Gloves</span></a> though, but I would suggest going for the 4-set bonus first,<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Glove Enchant</b>: <a class="q1 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=38967/enchant-gloves-major-agility">
<img alt="Enchant Gloves - Major Agility" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enchantedscroll.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Gloves - Major Agility</span></a>
<div class="pad"></div>
<div class="markup-table-wrapper">
<table class="grid max-width">
<tbody>
